column14:
While I agree the code presented is just, plain and simple, bad, and the first way to the solution is splitting it up, I really don&#x27;t get why you want comments for every line? Or don&#x27;t you mean literally every line maybe?<p>I mean suppose I split the first part of the statement like this:<p><pre><code>  int r = a[ i ];
  ++i;
</code></pre>
These lines are self-explanatory. It&#x27;s pretty hard to argue they need a comment? Especially when used in a function that already should have a name/comment explaining what it does?
